{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01393",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.78,
      "end_seconds": 9.02,
      "duration_seconds": 8.24,
      "text": "Hello doctor, um, sorry, I took a wrong turn on the way here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.87,
      "end_seconds": 15.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.55,
      "text": "Of course, leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 15.92,
      "end_seconds": 20.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.38,
      "end_seconds": 25.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 28.88,
      "end_seconds": 32.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "uh, we came because of bruising easily"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 33.61,
      "end_seconds": 36.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.56,
      "end_seconds": 41.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Around a week, um, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 43.29,
      "end_seconds": 47.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.95,
      "text": "Hm, I'd say more like two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.31,
      "end_seconds": 53.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly one to two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.46,
      "end_seconds": 56.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Yeah, roughly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.2,
      "end_seconds": 59.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 60.57,
      "end_seconds": 78.11,
      "duration_seconds": 17.54,
      "text": "Nose bleeds goes along with it, uh, most of the time. Erm, the Nose bleeds? That's been for six months. With Nose bleeds, maybe a eight out of ten on a bad day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.75,
      "end_seconds": 82.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Any indigestion after tablets as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.02,
      "end_seconds": 93.32,
      "duration_seconds": 10.3,
      "text": "so, yes, for two years uh, as for indigestion after tablets, I'd give it a eight, out of ten"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.67,
      "end_seconds": 96.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "what about your medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.4,
      "end_seconds": 110.61,
      "duration_seconds": 12.21,
      "text": "Ah, I have heart disease, for about a year. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.56,
      "end_seconds": 114.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Any surgery in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.63,
      "end_seconds": 127.99,
      "duration_seconds": 8.36,
      "text": "Uh, um, just a meniscus repair on my knee, four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.93,
      "end_seconds": 132.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.73,
      "end_seconds": 137.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Yes, cat fur, it gives me wheezing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.42,
      "end_seconds": 141.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 142.56,
      "end_seconds": 154.7,
      "duration_seconds": 12.14,
      "text": "I take clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day for the stent. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.99,
      "end_seconds": 165.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Do you get out much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.16,
      "end_seconds": 171.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "Not much, I mostly stay in these days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.11,
      "end_seconds": 173.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.61,
      "end_seconds": 179.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.62,
      "end_seconds": 184.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "do you work outside the home?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 185.66,
      "end_seconds": 189.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.7,
      "end_seconds": 194.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Does your family have any medical conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.07,
      "end_seconds": 197.05,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "My cousin has psoriasis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.59,
      "end_seconds": 208.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Have you noticed palpitations or blood in the urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.19,
      "end_seconds": 215.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.19,
      "text": "No palpitations or blood in the urine, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.08,
      "end_seconds": 219.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Have you noticed fainting or pain at rest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 221.52,
      "end_seconds": 227.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.78,
      "text": "So, um, no, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.3,
      "end_seconds": 234.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.09,
      "end_seconds": 237.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "nothing odd there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.19,
      "end_seconds": 240.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.1,
      "end_seconds": 242.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.15,
      "text": "breathing's normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.57,
      "end_seconds": 245.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.08,
      "end_seconds": 254.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Bear with me while this finishes..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.43,
      "end_seconds": 275.13,
      "duration_seconds": 9.7,
      "text": "Okay: weight 64 kilos, height 177 centimetres, blood pressure 115 over 77, BMI works out to 20.4, pulse 69."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.52,
      "end_seconds": 278.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Is that that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.76,
      "end_seconds": 287.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Alright, I'll interpret them after the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 289.02,
      "end_seconds": 293.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "alright, over here please and I'll take a look"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 294.3,
      "end_seconds": 295.0,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.59,
      "end_seconds": 298.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "Let me feel here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.7,
      "end_seconds": 314.57,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "There are a few small bruises on your forearms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.75,
      "end_seconds": 341.17,
      "duration_seconds": 21.42,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check. Okay, thinking it through, I'd lean towards stable coronary disease on antiplatelet treatment, with minor bleeding. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. It could also be angina, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 341.91,
      "end_seconds": 345.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Ah, uh, is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 346.35,
      "end_seconds": 360.64,
      "duration_seconds": 14.29,
      "text": "I understand the worry at the moment I'd say it's stable coronary disease on antiplatelet treatment, with minor bleeding, and we'll know more once the an ECG is back"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 371.71,
      "end_seconds": 377.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "Let's get an ECG, for chest discomfort. Let's get blood tests, for bruising and bleeding."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 379.59,
      "end_seconds": 381.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "That makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 382.5,
      "end_seconds": 408.24,
      "duration_seconds": 25.74,
      "text": "The treatment will be pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast, long term. It's for stomach protection. The pharmacy will go through the details again when you pick it up. Take your blood-thinning tablets after food and do not stop them on your own. Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 409.44,
      "end_seconds": 416.34,
      "duration_seconds": 6.9,
      "text": "Let me think, you know, can you send me for a lipid profile?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 417.47,
      "end_seconds": 437.83,
      "duration_seconds": 20.36,
      "text": "I wouldn't order it today. If anything changes, we'll reconsider. One warning sign to remember: you pass black stools or have prolonged bleeding. In that case don't wait. Book a review after the blood results. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 439.47,
      "end_seconds": 443.92,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Okay, that that makes sense. Thanks for explaining."
    }
  ]
}